                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "300 m DK cotton in total. For a single-colour runner, three 100 m balls of the same colour. For a multi-colour runner, 8 m per square = approx. 320 m across as many colours as needed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished granny square measures 9 × 9 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook, lightly blocked."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring (MR)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr). UK term; US equivalent is double crochet (dc)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Granny cluster: 3 tr into a ch-2 corner space"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Granny square (make 40)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "MR: ch 3 (counts as tr), 2 tr, ch 2, *3 tr, ch 2; repeat 3 more times, sl st to top of ch 3 to join (4 clusters, 4 ch-2 corner spaces)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: sl st to ch-2 corner space. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr into same corner space (first corner). *Ch 1, [3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr] into next corner space; repeat from * twice, ch 1, sl st to top of ch 3 (8 clusters: 2 per corner + 4 ch-1 side spaces)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 3: sl st to ch-2 corner. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr into corner. *Ch 1, 3 tr into side ch-1 space, ch 1, [3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr] into next corner; repeat from * 3 times, omitting last corner on final repeat, sl st to top of ch 3 (12 clusters: 2 per corner + 2 per side). Fasten off."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Arrange 40 squares in a 4-wide × 10-long grid. Hold two squares wrong sides together and work a sl st seam along one edge through both outer loops. Join squares row by row, 4 squares across, then join the rows lengthwise. The seam sits on the right side as a small raised ridge; reverse the direction alternately to prevent the runner from curling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends: there will be at least 2 per square (40 squares = 80 ends minimum). Light wet-blocking on a mat evens the squares and flattens the seams. Pin to size and leave until dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine-wash on 30°C gentle cycle. Lay flat to dry. The cotton softens slightly with each wash."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}